  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 1.0.23, package.json says 1.0.0.",
        "  The App Store and the server read info.xml; everything on the node side reads package.json. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying two version numbers, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml states no <repository>.",
        "  <repository> is the only machine-readable link from a published release back to the source it was built from, and <bugs> is where the App Store page sends a report. Without them a user of the release has no way back to the project."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "link-dead",
      "lines": [
        "5 links of appinfo/info.xml lead nowhere:",
        "  <website> https://eID.services/eidlogin/nextcloud: HTTP 404, after a redirect to https://www.eid.services/eidlogin/nextcloud",
        "  <bugs> https://eID.services/eidlogin/nextcloud/bugs: HTTP 404, after a redirect to https://www.eid.services/eidlogin/nextcloud/bugs",
        "  <documentation><user> https://eID.services/eidlogin/nextcloud/userdocs?lang=en: HTTP 404, after a redirect to https://www.eid.services/eidlogin/nextcloud/userdocs?lang=en",
        "  <documentation><admin> https://eID.services/eidlogin/nextcloud/admindocs?lang=en: HTTP 404, after a redirect to https://www.eid.services/eidlogin/nextcloud/admindocs?lang=en",
        "  <documentation><developer> https://eID.services/eidlogin/nextcloud/devdocs?lang=en: HTTP 404, after a redirect to https://www.eid.services/eidlogin/nextcloud/devdocs?lang=en",
        "  The App Store page shows these links as they are; a reader who follows one ends on an error page."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0-or-later (package.json), AGPL (composer.json).",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 33 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead.",
        "  No SPDX id: AGPL (composer.json). Only an SPDX id says which licence is meant, and for a GNU licence whether -only or -or-later.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is eidlogin, the checkout directory is eid-login-nextcloud.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "link-redirect",
      "lines": [
        "3 links of appinfo/info.xml have moved permanently:",
        "  <screenshot> https://eID.services/assets/img/Title-Nextcloud-de.png",
        "    now https://www.eid.services/assets/img/Title-Nextcloud-de.png",
        "  <screenshot> https://eID.services/assets/img/nextcloud-appstore/Login-Nextcloud-de.png",
        "    now https://www.eid.services/assets/img/nextcloud-appstore/Login-Nextcloud-de.png",
        "  <screenshot> https://eID.services/assets/img/nextcloud-appstore/Wizard-Nextcloud-de.png",
        "    now https://www.eid.services/assets/img/nextcloud-appstore/Wizard-Nextcloud-de.png",
        "  The old address works only as long as the redirect is kept; the new one can be stated directly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
        "PHP floor stated once: appinfo/info.xml min-version 7.4; composer.json states no php requirement.",
        "  Nothing contradicts anything here. Stating it in both places is what keeps a composer install from resolving packages for a PHP the server will not run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node stated as >=14.0.0 (package.json engines.node).",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (.eslintrc.js, superseded form), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php), EditorConfig (.editorconfig).",
        " ESLint is configured in .eslintrc.js: ESLint 9 reads the flat config only; the eslintrc form, an .eslintrc file or the eslintConfig key in package.json, is ignored unless the run is pinned to ESLint 8.",
        " No Stylelint configuration: stylesheets are unchecked, and a mistake in CSS fails silently instead of loudly.",
        " No PHPUnit configuration: there is no test harness in the checkout, so nothing can be run against a change.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "1 declared package is named nowhere in the checkout: @nextcloud/eslint-plugin.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 74 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 33 to 35; the oldest maintained major is 32 (as of 2026-09), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "lockfiles",
      "lines": [
        "package-lock.json (lockfileVersion 3) and composer.lock in the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "ncmake-bootstrap",
      "lines": [
        "The ncmake bootstrap stub is in place (21 lines)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "Every directory the shipped PHP reaches through __DIR__ and the frontend through linkTo is in the shipped file set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk)."
      ]
    }
  ],
